{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/303168-bitching-about-players-thread","id":303168,"title":"Bitching About Players Thread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-05T03:31:49-08:00","id":303168,"title":"Bitching About Players Thread","content":"In the spirit of the Bitching About ST Thread I bring the other side of the coin! A place for the ST's complain about their players and for players to learn a few things.<br /> <br /> Since I don't ST I leave you with &quot;The Michelle Chronicles&quot; from the old forums which is the true accounts of funny gaming sessions that Marc the Draconian Garden Gnome (patron Saint of patient Storytellers) had to put up with.<br /> <br /> Completely hilarious: <a href=\"http://www.angelfire.com/rpg/michelle/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.angelfire.com/rpg/michelle/</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2435-prophet","name":"Prophet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2435_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T10:10:17-08:00","id":303376,"title":"","content":"Sorry, but I have to gripe about my one time running a <b>Hunter: the Reckoning</b> game. It was shortly after the game came out and put me off being an ST for a couple of years. Yeah, it was that bad.<br /> <br /> Since it was shortly after the game came out, I was dealing with a bunch of players that were accustomed to playing nigh-unkillable vampires and werewolves and mages, which I think contributed to a lot of the problems. I am not the kind of ST to keep PCs alive just because they're the PCs. If they do something monumentally stupid, sorry, your character died. I ran 3 sessions of the game, everybody had to make another character by the middle of the second session. Some died in the first session. I wasn't throwing anything major at them, just PC level monsters that they'd been able to deal with before..........as supernatural monsters themselves. I was hoping that by the third session, it would sink in that they were mortals fighting things that were way more poerful and they'd have to start getting clever and creative and work as a team to take them down. Silly me.<br /> <br /> The incident that made me stand up and declare the game over was our resident &quot;Wolverine wanna be, I always gotta to face the bad guys by myself&quot;. After some (but still not all) of the players decided that working together might not be a bad idea, this putz still has to tell me his character is going to go off to the warehouse where they think a monster is hiding and take it on himself. Despite my warnings about it being a bad idea, he insists.<br /> <br /> His character drives to the warehouse, breaks into the place.....noisily....and starts flashing his light around to find something. He discovers a homeless guy and HITS him until he wakes up. He decides to start badgering him about being the monster or seeing something. Turns out the first part was right. He's a Bone Gnawer Ahroun camped out there to keep an eye on a Pentex facility nearby. The PC unloads a few rounds from a handgun and runs back to his car. I was hoping it was to flee back to his friends because he realized it was a bad idea. Nope, pops the trunk for his shotgun and turns back to see the werewolf slowly coming out to get him. I was trying to be nice and let him get away, so I say &quot;50 feet away&quot;. He fires, werewolf keeps coming. &quot;40 feet away&quot;, he fires, werewolf keeps coming. 30 feet, 20 feet.....10....5.....he just keeps standing there firing and reloading. In total frustration, I stand up and declare that the werewolf has ripped him apart and that the other members of his pack were alerted the second he entered the warehouse and they were busy tracking him back to his base and found the other hunters there and ripped them all apart, too. Game over, man, game over! Everybody go home!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Fortunately, the NWOD made the PCs a little more vulnerable, so I haven't encountered this since.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T13:37:46-08:00","id":303699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fortunately, the NWOD made the PCs a little more vulnerable, so I haven't encountered this since. </div> </div> </div>Jesus Christ, since I got into NWoD I cannot look at 6/4/3 mortal attributes spread of OWoD seriously, because that feels too much. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T20:29:15-08:00","id":304101,"title":"","content":"I can never truly complain about my players from any game. They are all far more sane than I, and trusted hours of their time and mental energy to my fever-dream-written stories and homemade madness. I can only think of them as heroes. True Heroes Are They, That Trusted My Dice. Saints Among Men, Through Story They Fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T03:18:57-08:00","id":304378,"title":"","content":"@Papa Bear ALL PCs are vulnerable, no exception. And I play Exalted!<br /> <br /> Still, the problem wasn't the game but the closed mentality of the players. When I played Dark Ages Inquisitor, we got to a point the group was powerful, had overpowered relics and still we approached the supernatural monsters with caution, even my hot headed Poor Knight! <br /> <br /> Although that Inquisitor Chronicle had me nerdraging against a fellow PC. There was a Vampire immobilized by a holy power (can't recall which one) and I was pinned down by a ghoul with Potence breaking my bones and my dear friend and Poor Knight comrade moves in for the kill, takes the vampire's head with glory as I give up my last breath with the Ghoul smashing my had Mountain - Oberan Style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2435-prophet","name":"Prophet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2435_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T03:21:19-08:00","id":304380,"title":"","content":"My players/co-players are too psycho to handle them without a Henderson tier derail.<br /> <br /> So looking forward to Karen raping that poor Demon. Literally. Because she wants to have a mix blooded off-spring for eugenics program. She expressed recently disappointment in not managing to dissect that True Fae whom our knife nut killed with one stab.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile my PC goes around dressed as a Catholic priest to &quot;fool&quot; a local Angel. And he is the sanest cellmate in spite of believing that Angels are cyborgs sent by US government.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":2918,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","user":"Kat","date":". 11-06-2014, 06:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T06:43:10-08:00","id":304535,"title":"","content":"Let's see. There was the guy playing an Assamite who insisted the Path of Blood obliged him to hurl himself bodily off a cliff after a lower-gen vampire, and insisted the ST should cut him some slack on that whole gravity thing. And then buried a knife in the table when he turned into a red smear on the ground.<br /> <br /> There was the guy who played a monstrously offensive hibachi chef trying to make new flavors of blood.<br /> <br /> There was the guy who took the approach that if they shouted anything loud enough it would become patently awesome to everyone at the table. <br /> <br /> Then there was the cast from my Exalted game:<br /> The one who by the end of the second session had become his player's mouthpiece on how boned the world was and all the things that needed to be done to save it (&quot;I think we need to find our Lunar mates and go to Yu-shan&quot; was on the list, despite none of these having been mentioned before.)<br /> There was the player running an online game, who would bring her laptop, do stuff with her other game while sitting in the background of what was going on, browse the web, and at least once burst out laughing mid-session to show everyone the Lego bible.<br /> There were the players who didn't do ANYTHING. One had the sole function of &quot;I have a boat&quot; and I cannot tell you a single facet of her personality. The other actually had a good character when she showed up and occasionally did stuff, but like the other she was there to be sociable, and would often tune things out to play on her DS or knit.<br /> There was the woman who quit repeatedly.<br /> There was the guy who first made a Killfuck Soulshitter before that was a meme, and then when we all realized he was a poor fit, made a new character who was blandly useful as a Fighter, and spent most of his time in Great Forks.<br /> <br /> And then..Hoo boy.<br /> <br /> All right, so this is where things really went south for my Exalted game. Owing to inter-player strife and/or deciding to get married and move to Denmark, the players invested in the story and bearing plot hooks had all left. I had a new player waiting in the wings, though, so I was willing to keep trying.<br /> <br /> To his credit, he's enthusiastic and tries to keep involved. However, like one of the guys mentioned above he's loud, kind of obnoxious, grabs the spotlight, and occasionally misses the point entirely--like when he decided to play a Lunar, upon realizing Lunar Exalted were--in 2e--civilization-builders, he tried to make a whole eugenically-formed nation Dragon-blooded, and pass this off as an unambiguously good thing.<br /> <br /> when we moved onto Scion, he tried to stay in the spotlight at all times; when a government agency started looking at them sideways, he wanted to be the awesome guy who tracked them down, knocked on their door, and told them in no uncertain terms how things were going to go. He was PAINFULLY put out when the character who had actually been an agent in her backstory, without prompting or encouragement, initiated contact on her own and made for a much more cordial state of affairs.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure I could go on, but it's not 100% fair to the people who subject themselves to my whim, and also typing all this out on a phone is a little more laborious than I'd like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T06:54:22-08:00","id":304540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prophet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/303168-bitching-about-players-thread?p=304378#post304378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Papa Bear ALL PCs are vulnerable, no exception. And I play Exalted!<br /> <br /> Still, the problem wasn't the game but the closed mentality of the players.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is what I think, too, which is why I was bitching about the players not the game.<br /> <br /> It's taken some time for a lot of RPG players to get over to the mentality of &quot;your character can die, too, y'know.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T08:49:36-08:00","id":304630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/303168-bitching-about-players-thread?p=304535#post304535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's see. There was the guy playing an Assamite who insisted the Path of Blood obliged him to hurl himself bodily off a cliff after a lower-gen vampire, and insisted the ST should cut him some slack on that whole gravity thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Loved this one. Although the knife part sounds a bit too psycho... not very mentally stable the fellow.<br /> <br /> @Papa Bear Exactly. One game I missed of D&amp;D, my friends were epic level characters and they ran away from a Kobold because all their powers told them it was just Kobold and their thought was &quot;This is some powerful shit, none of our powers work. Better go away and do not make him mad.&quot; LoL The DM had the time of his life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2435-prophet","name":"Prophet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2435_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T11:14:14-08:00","id":304745,"title":"","content":"^We have exactly opposite attitude in DnD. We try to kill everything that looks nasty and moves, even if clearly outmatche.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T11:42:39-08:00","id":304803,"title":"","content":"I don't really want to trash any of my players, but I will share a collection of stories about idiotic shadowrunners:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.highprogrammer.com/alan/gaming/shadowrun/clue-files.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.highprogrammer.com/alan/gaming/shadowrun/clue-files.html\" target=\"_blank\"> Shadowrun C.L.U.E. Files </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.highprogrammer.com/alan/gaming/shadowrun/clue-files.html\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.highprogrammer.com/alan/gaming/shadowrun/clue-files.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T12:00:59-08:00","id":304833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prophet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/303168-bitching-about-players-thread?p=304630#post304630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although the knife part sounds a bit too psycho... not very mentally stable the fellow.</div> </div> </div> </div>He wasn't. He could be friendly and generous, but was very clearly always high-strung and was always smiling in a way that just had too many teeth, if you get my meaning. <br /> <br /> He was also a relentless powergamer who insisted he had fantastic luck with dice, as shown by his rolling, quickly picking up a bunch, and then saying that the ones he was holding in his hand were his successes.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T12:01:59-08:00","id":304834,"title":"","content":"I personally enjoy introducing Killstick McFuckyou players to the old Paranoia rpg. I just don't fell them I've changed games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T12:13:51-08:00","id":304867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/303168-bitching-about-players-thread?p=304745#post304745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">^We have exactly opposite attitude in DnD. We try to kill everything that looks nasty and moves, even if clearly outmatche.</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as you never face the dreaded gazebo, you'll be fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T17:05:34-08:00","id":305115,"title":"","content":"I killed off bodyguard in a duel of a fatman who turned out to be a member of grand council and escaped to sewers. At least I got shitload of XP for that because NPC was twice stronger than me but I punched him to death anyway.<br /> <br /> And that rich guy thinks other PC killed me, so other player got prize for my head (without showing body because he rolled natural 20 on Bluff) and I'm officially dead. I will wait in wilderness for others to catch up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T11:02:50-08:00","id":305946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/303168-bitching-about-players-thread?p=304535#post304535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then there was the cast from my Exalted game:<br /> The one who by the end of the second session had become his player's mouthpiece on how boned the world was and all the things that needed to be done to save it (&quot;I think we need to find our Lunar mates and go to Yu-shan&quot; was on the list, despite none of these having been mentioned before.)<br /> There was the player running an online game, who would bring her laptop, do stuff with her other game while sitting in the background of what was going on, browse the web, and at least once burst out laughing mid-session to show everyone the Lego bible.<br /> There were the players who didn't do ANYTHING. One had the sole function of &quot;I have a boat&quot; and I cannot tell you a single facet of her personality. The other actually had a good character when she showed up and occasionally did stuff, but like the other she was there to be sociable, and would often tune things out to play on her DS or knit.<br /> There was the woman who quit repeatedly.<br /> There was the guy who first made a Killfuck Soulshitter before that was a meme, and then when we all realized he was a poor fit, made a new character who was blandly useful as a Fighter, and spent most of his time in Great Forks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Jesus christ this sounds exactly like my original gaming group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T11:25:15-08:00","id":305994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There were the players who didn't do ANYTHING. One had the sole function of &quot;I have a boat&quot; and I cannot tell you a single facet of her personality. </div> </div> </div>Our boat owner is at least very moe young lass with a cute small crocodile as a pet.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T09:03:07-08:00","id":335235,"title":"","content":"Found another archive - this one is the experiences of Vampire: The Masquerade group with someone name <a href=\"http://www.angelfire.com/rpg/michelle/\" target=\"_blank\">Michelle</a>, who really should never have stayed past the first session.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T10:38:08-08:00","id":335320,"title":"","content":"MIchelle's &quot;adventures&quot; were already linked in the first post of this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T03:54:15-08:00","id":336894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/303168-bitching-about-players-thread?p=335235#post335235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Found another archive - this one is the experiences of Vampire: The Masquerade group with someone name <a href=\"http://www.angelfire.com/rpg/michelle/\" target=\"_blank\">Michelle</a>, who really should never have stayed past the first session.</div> </div> </div> </div>This... this is amazing. I have no words for this, only laughter. I really wish I could meet Marc and bring him a 6 pack of beer and congratulate him for 4+ years of Michelle. It's also a massive relief to see that me and my friends aren't doing so bad, being new to the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4292-lumina","name":"Lumina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T15:45:40-08:00","id":337463,"title":"","content":"Oh, my goodness -- Michelle. I remember when that shit first got posted back in the late 90's, whatever incarnation of the forum ago. That shit is *the* Bible of Bad/Shit Players, or at the very least a prominent chapter in said Bible. Awesome shit...<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T18:47:37-08:00","id":337621,"title":"","content":"I had one player in a VtM game fail so hard that he rage quit the game.<br /> <br /> First character was a Ventrue who was trying to be Batman. He was a detective and like Fortitude. A lot. I had the Houserule in place before it was even a concept in DAV20 for Fort so he abused Fort a lot. First session is that there is a Sabbat street war going on in the city and some Sabbat need to be killed by the group by order of the Prince. So the Ventrue walks into the street and just starts converting blood into wasted bullets as snipers start pinging him and doing nothing. Rest of the group meanwhile just uses cover and shit and get to the snipers while the Ventrue lights it on fire. Frenzy every where and lots of dead humans.<br /> Next session is where he lost it. He decided to torture another PC who was a Highlander, because fuck you you're weird and I instead of asking questions I'm going to torture you and your 10 Willpower. Finally let the Highlander go and gave him his sword back before retiring for the day. Highlander goes and steals a van, fills it with 300 gallons of gasoline and drive through the front door where the Ventrue is having an Orgie after he diablerized another PC just 6 hours prior. Highlander walks away and hits the explode button and I roll damage. He blows Forts and barely survives by good luck and being covered in lots of bodies. He runs through the burning building and escapes into the sewers with 4 blood points and stacking several wounds. He climbs out of a manhole on the outskirts of town and doesn't put the cover back on. I have a car drive over it and crash into a telephone pole nearby and he sees a man stumble out of it. He proceeds to see if the people in are awake and then tries to attack the man and feed on him. Guy manages to fight him off. Thus begins the most hilarious fist fight in the history of my games. This Vampire with 4 Stamina and 4 Fort begins to lose to a mundane human mook. After about 3 minutes of fighting and the guy saving his kids, after having his own gun pulled on him by the Ventrue the fight ends with this Vampire in Torpor in the middle of the street. Yeah he lost to a human. It gets worse from there as his character dies to the Sabbat after they shove a bomb into his chest and the Highlander botches the disarm roll on the bomb after he walked into a popular mall with the bomb in his chest. 10lbs of C4 level bomb.<br /> <br /> His next character was even more terrible. He was a Toreador that couldn't charm anyone without Presence and owned a night club. Basically he broke the Masquerade 4 times in one night and pretty much told the press that his club sells drugs to patrons. This character died after he told a whole strip club he's a Vampire in front of the Toreador Primogen. He rage quit after that because he didn't think he was punished correctly by losing just his arm.<br /> <br /> I have no idea what he was thinking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":2414,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","user":"theoutlander523","date":". 12-11-2014, 10:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T21:44:37-08:00","id":337716,"title":"","content":"Ahhh yes, the Daeva player who played the Vice of Sloth. As. Literally. As. <b>Possible</b>.<br /> <br /> Call to adventure? She reads a book!<br /> The plot thickens? She goes home!<br /> <br /> (For those who don't know, the Daeva clan weakness in first edition <b>Requiem </b>was that they lost two points of Willpower for not indulging their Vices.)<br /> <br /> This wasn't player apathy. This was the player purposely portraying the <i>character </i>to be as apathetic as possible, because that particular novelty concept was more important than just about anything else happening in the chronicle. The player was playing the <i>hell </i>out of this character, and that was neither fun nor compelling to anyone else in the troupe, and more often than not ended up being disruptive. There was no growth; there was only dogged, <i>bizarre </i>dedication to this frustrating character.<br /> <br /> Now, it was my first time STing , so I was green as hell. I probably could've dealt with it better than I did...but even with experience, I honestly still don't know how that could've been interesting.<br /> <br /> This player had other...quirks. Ask me about <b>The Cat Story</b> at your own peril.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T01:37:53-08:00","id":337883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/303168-bitching-about-players-thread?p=337716#post337716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Ask me about <b>The Cat Story</b> at your own peril.</div> </div> </div> </div>If this is anything like Michelle you're under an obligation to tell it, don't deny the world stories like that!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4292-lumina","name":"Lumina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T02:42:46-08:00","id":337898,"title":"","content":"Yossarian, could you please tell us about the Cat Story? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T03:16:43-08:00","id":337908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lumina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/303168-bitching-about-players-thread?p=337883#post337883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If this is anything like Michelle you're under an obligation to tell it, don't deny the world stories like that!</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/303168-bitching-about-players-thread?p=337883#post337883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yossarian, could you please tell us about the Cat Story?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, very well...but tomorrow. I need to give it the detail it deserves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T14:56:31-08:00","id":338479,"title":"","content":"My caveat is that this story is immensely stupid.<br /> <br /> Little background first:<br /> <br /> The chronicle was core nWoD, first edition. We were playing psychic spies, employed by an underfunded section of the British Secret Service, circa 1960. Our main antagonist was Blue Star, an equivalent Soviet agency. They were significantly better funded, and their psychics were abnormally powerful. This is one of the best chronicles I've ever been in. The Storyteller masterfully crafted the setting and the missions, and there was genuine drama every time a character thought he might get caught. Character death was a looming threat. We had to make hard moral choices; we had to engage with the system. The whole thing exemplified everything I love about the Storytelling System and the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Except.<br /> <br /> This guy. This player. He was the Daeva from above. He got into this game by inviting himself into it, and none of us having the heart to tell him no. We thought he'd be better this time.<br /> <br /> <b>The Cat Story</b><br /> <br /> We were in Paris, trying to track down a potential asset (i.e., another psychic). Without going into too much detail, we set up an operation to extract the psychic, but we knew that Blue Star was onto us. The player, who we will call &quot;Bob&quot;, was our sniper. He had a psychic power, but it's not germane to this. While the rest of the team went to capture this psychic, Bob's character set up a sniper's nest, just in case any Soviets showed up. To make a long story short, they sort of did, right as we captured the psychic. One of our agents ended up being mind controlled by a powerful Soviet psychic. His player managed to knock himself out before Blue Star could use that to their advantage, and ended up passed out in our getaway van, along with my character <i>and </i>the captured psychic. The Soviets didn't know exactly where we were, or where our escape van was, but they were closing in fast. No enemy agents have shown up physically.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Bob decided to make his way down, because shit is hitting the fan and we have to get the hell out of dodge. His character knows that we have two agents in the van, and the acquired psychic.<br /> <br /> He gets down to the street, and he sees a <b>cat</b>. One of our antagonists, who we met in the previous session, had the power to possess animals. The cat immediately attacked him, so we're fairly certain that's what's happening. The cat is more or less grappling him. Bob tries to fight off the cat, but it won't get off him. He manages to stagger near our van, where all our everything is located.<br /> <br /> <b>Bob</b>: &quot;I'm going to get in the van.&quot;<br /> <br /> One of the other players (we'll call him &quot;Ben&quot;) suggests that letting the cat in the van would be a bad idea, for a variety of reasons, most pertinent of all being that the Soviet possessing the cat would see everything, would know where we were, and very likely be able to track us and kill us.<br /> <br /> So, Ben suggests that maybe Bob should just throw the cat against the van to stun it or kill it.<br /> <br /> Bob says he won't kill the cat.<br /> <br /> Ben says, okay, fine, but don't put it in the van. We all kind of nodded at this point.<br /> <br /> Bob says he won't kill the cat.<br /> <br /> Ben says it's not about killing the cat. Bob doesn't need to kill the cat. It's about the characters protecting themselves. &quot;Your character would know this would be a huge mistake.&quot;<br /> <br /> Bob says he won't kill the cat.<br /> <br /> Ben says, okay, fine, but don't put it in the damn van.<br /> <br /> <b>Bob says he won't kill the cat.</b><br /> <br /> If that's confusing to you, imagine how we felt.<br /> <br /> What proceeded was the most acrimonious dispute I've ever seen at a gaming table. He couldn't let go of the mere suggestion that killing the cat was an option, long, long, long after anyone was seriously suggesting it. Once it was clear, we understood that this was triggering to him. I completely understand why the death of an animal could be upsetting, even for pretend. I myself am deeply affected by it when it happens in TV and movies. But at no point was anyone <i>pushing </i>for him to kill the cat. It was blindingly evident that he didn't want to do that. We really just wanted him to not put it in the van. That's all. Even the Storyteller pointed out that putting the cat in the van was a very bad choice. But every time we tried to end the discussion, to let it go, Bob would bring it up again, expressly to continue the argument. He insisted on couching it in terms of his character, rather than himself, and tried to argue for the logic of letting it be in the van.<br /> <br /> Ben later admitted that he contributed to the length of the argument, and got way too angry about it, but at the time he was apoplectic that Bob, who'd invited himself into the game, was now going to result in everyone's death, and ruin what had been a genuinely awesome chronicle.<br /> <br /> <b>Bob</b>: &quot;You're all a bunch of dicks.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Ben</b>: &quot;You don't need to kill the cat! I'm not saying you have to do that! But you aren't recognizing why this is a problem because you won't listen to me!&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Bob</b>: &quot;I won't kill a cat over this!&quot; &lt;-- Direct quote<br /> <br /> <b>Me (who up to this point was too mortified to say anything)</b>: &quot;It's an imaginary fucking cat!&quot;<br /> <br /> At this point, the Storyteller didn't really grasp the situation. He just thought it was annoying, and wanted to move on. To end the discussion, he ruled that the cat would simply die after it was finished being possessed. This wasn't malice or pettiness, this was just the ST wanting to get the hell on with it. He didn't realise this was a player thing, not a character thing.<br /> <br /> <b>Bob</b>: &quot;You're a moron.&quot;<br /> <br /> This ST is one of my closest friends. He's one of the nicest, kindest men I know. I've never heard anyone say a bad thing about him. And I've never seen him angry.<br /> <br /> Except for that moment. I don't know how he had the composure to do this, but rather than telling Bob to get the hell out of the house, he ruled that the possession on the cat ended, and that it was no longer attacking him, and that it was running away. Bob finally stopped bringing it up. Somehow, we finished the session.<br /> <br /> This was the single worst experience I've ever had in an RPG.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 12-12-2014, 07:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T15:31:46-08:00","id":338510,"title":"","content":"I can understand reacting poorly to triggers (I ban certain things in my games, period) but that &quot;Bob&quot; was an ass from begining to end. Who the hell autoinvites to a long going game, for starters?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T16:04:25-08:00","id":338527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ahhh yes, the Daeva player who played the Vice of Sloth. As. Literally. As. Possible.<br /> <br /> Call to adventure? She reads a book!<br /> The plot thickens? She goes home!<br /> <br /> (For those who don't know, the Daeva clan weakness in first edition Requiem was that they lost two points of Willpower for not indulging their Vices.)<br /> <br /> This wasn't player apathy. This was the player purposely portraying the character to be as apathetic as possible, because that particular novelty concept was more important than just about anything else happening in the chronicle. The player was playing the hell out of this character, and that was neither fun nor compelling to anyone else in the troupe, and more often than not ended up being disruptive. There was no growth; there was only dogged, bizarre dedication to this frustrating character.<br /> <br /> Now, it was my first time STing , so I was green as hell. I probably could've dealt with it better than I did...but even with experience, I honestly still don't know how that could've been interesting.<br /> <br /> This player had other...quirks. Ask me about The Cat Story at your own peril. </div> </div> </div>In my case, it's like Mike all over again except that Mike is actually indecisive, rather than portraying his characters apathetic on purpose.<br /> <br /> Holy Mother, in one play by post RPG thousands of messages in Skype chat and two days were spent on him arguing with us about one thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T08:35:09-08:00","id":339082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>theoutlander523</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/303168-bitching-about-players-thread?p=337621#post337621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had one player in a VtM game fail so hard that he rage quit the game.<br /> <br /> [...]<br /> <br /> I have no idea what he was thinking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah... that dude sounded like he had issues. (PCs killing/diablerizing other PCs, while I've seen it occur in some rare games over the past going on 25 years, is something that usually leaves a bad taste in people's mouths... so to speak...; couple with his other actions, it's amazing his characters hadn't died earlier in their respective scenarios. And the Toreador losing an arm? Sure, for the *character* that would be annoying as hell, but on the player level he should have been like &quot;Wow -- that's it? -- [Character name] sure lucked out on that one...&quot;, especially as -- barring a couple Thaumaturgical/high-end Vicissitude powers, the RAW allow him to regenerate the arm fairly easily, barring being in torpor and without blood.) Sounds like a dick. Did he ever game with you/your people again? (Just curious...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T20:40:50-08:00","id":347972,"title":"","content":"I had a player back when I ran vtm. He was obsessed with the sabbat, and specifically the losambra. He was antagonist to the other players and just so argumentative. He insisted that every rule be straight out of the book but I swore he never read any. Every time I cited a page source he'd run out if the house screaming about how &quot;it wasn't the book he was talking about&quot; then he'd come back and say he only got upset because he wasn't allowed to get stoned during my games. It was the last owod game I ever ran and had to take a break from storytelling all together. It wasn't until sin-eater came out that I actuaaly had the desire to run a game again. He wasn't invited back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T01:48:58-08:00","id":348125,"title":"","content":"Taht due was on heavy ****... I'm sure it wasn't just on grass he was getting high xD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2435-prophet","name":"Prophet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2435_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-20T11:20:47-08:00","id":376449,"title":"","content":"Oh man, one dude in our HtV game...<br /> <br /> If his characters weren't being stupid, they were being incredibly stubborn. Whenever the rest of us tried get him out of whatever &quot;special&quot; thing he wanted to do (it was always stupid) so we can move the game along he always contested the rolls. Every. Single. Time.<br /> <br /> He got us surrounded by a SWAT team just after we came out of a vampire bar, ate some goblin fruits in the Hedge, wandered off so many times I've lost count, decided to resist not taking an injection that would prevent him from taking full lethal (I have no idea why), disregards a powerful vampire's death threat and (surprise!) someone ends up dead because of it, blurted out our mission objective right in the target's faces in one mission (yes, face<i>s</i>, plural, as in multiple targets), and then there's his most recent antics...<br /> <br /> Alright, so a bunch of cargo ships have been mysteriously disappearing as of late. Being hunters, we decide to check it out of course, so we board the ship from our makeshift boat and more or less find out what's going on with the ships. Long story short: The ships were being taken to some alternate dimension that turned the crew into dehydrated zombies. The only reason why we weren't affected is because we had a special kind of &quot;sunscreen&quot; on. It wouldn't last forever though, so we had to get the hell outta dodge. We did, barely. However, the exit to the dimension we came out of left us stranded in some random part of the ocean.<br /> <br /> Naturally, we try to navigate our way to some land to figure things out from there. As we're doing that, we come across the Lochness Monster (or at least the equivalent of it). So what's our response to our current predicament? Full speed ahead in the opposite direction of course, except for this guy. He gets the bright idea to take a dip into the waters (shark-infested waters, by the way, we know because we got attacked by one and killed it, so there's lots of blood in there, too) and <i>swims towards the damn thing!</i><br /> <br /> Oh, it gets worse. Being a good cellmate, I decided to save him, which required a Strength + Athletics roll. Get this: My character's Strength and Athletics are both 1, so that's just a measly two dice and yes, I did know I had to make this roll before I even said I was gonna do it, but I obviously needed to do it anyways so I spend a Willpower. What does he do?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://youtu.be/PwqznmcFiWo?t=2h26m10s\" target=\"_blank\"><b>HE FUCKING CONTESTS MY ROLL!</b></a>(My character's name is Eulalia, his character's name is Ione)<br /> <br /> A roll I'm spending Willpower on to save his ass, and he wants to contest it (it's important to note that every time he contested my rolls when I was trying to prevent him from doing something stupid before this, he would win. Every time. So I thought for sure he was gonna win this roll, too. This is why I let out a big &quot;Thank God!&quot; after I won the roll). No, he wants to do something special. Why?<br /> <br /> Because our ST decided to make it so that our characters wouldn't die in the first season (our chronicle will have multiple seasons), so he gets the bright idea that as long as our characters are safe from death with the training wheels on, he might as well have fun with it. Yeah, and completely disregard the difficult position you're putting the ST in. Okay, so maybe our ST shouldn't have told any of us that, but she didn't anticipate the knowledge would be abused like this.<br /> <br /> Yeah, this guy's officially our group's Michelle...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-20T13:46:30-08:00","id":376578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/303168-bitching-about-players-thread?p=376449#post376449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because our ST decided to make it so that our characters wouldn't die in the first season (our chronicle will have multiple seasons), so he gets the bright idea that as long as our characters are safe from death with the training wheels on, he might as well have fun with it. Yeah, and completely disregard the difficult position you're putting the ST in. Okay, so maybe our ST shouldn't have told any of us that, but she didn't anticipate the knowledge would be abused like this.<br /> <br /> Yeah, this guy's officially our group's Michelle...</div> </div> </div> </div>This is how people end up Pledged, Gentrynapped, blood-addicted, ridden, cannibalized for Promethean parts or experimented on.<br /> <br /> It would be interesting if the ST lets this happen.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-20T14:57:19-08:00","id":376634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/303168-bitching-about-players-thread?p=376578#post376578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is how people end up Pledged, Gentrynapped, blood-addicted, ridden, cannibalized for Promethean parts or experimented on.<br /> <br /> It would be interesting if the ST lets this happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would, but I don't think she's gonna. At least, not in the first season anyways, and next session we start the season finale. After that, I'm officially gonna keep a death counter for how many character deaths (or whatever would equate to a character death as well, considering the aforementioned conditions along with others) he's gonna suffer in season two onwards if he keeps this up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-20T15:17:29-08:00","id":376645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/303168-bitching-about-players-thread?p=376634#post376634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would, but I don't think she's gonna. At least, not in the first season anyways, and next session we start the season finale. After that, I'm officially gonna keep a death counter for how many character deaths (or whatever would equate to a character death as well, considering the aforementioned conditions along with others) he's gonna suffer in season two onwards if he keeps this up.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's also the genie lamp.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T20:32:21-08:00","id":377747,"title":"","content":"Am I the only one reading through these, half-suspecting to find a story about me in here? Thankfully, none of the stupid shit I've done seems to have made it on here yet.<br /> <br /> There's a guy in one group I game with, great guy to hang out with and game with, but he is one of those people who think that lots of dots in Occult/Lore/whatever mean &quot;you know what's in the books&quot;. This has caused a few issues, like his character inevitably seeking out Mages in our NWoD games for their information-gathering abilities and convincing them to do the legwork, rather than engaging with the stories himself. Oddly enough, this only sporadically translates to when he's ST-ing. This is really annoying to me, because I like to try to get into my characters head and do what they would do given the knowledge they have, which unfortunately does sometimes mean they do something I know is stupid, and it's really hard to maintain that headspace if you've got a character sitting there spouting off about the ins and outs of vampire biology (necrology?).<br /> <br /> I mean, it's efficient, I guess, but just seems... lame? Not the right word, but I can't think of one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-24T08:16:15-08:00","id":380118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/303168-bitching-about-players-thread?p=377747#post377747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I the only one reading through these, half-suspecting to find a story about me in here? Thankfully, none of the stupid shit I've done seems to have made it on here yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everyone has done stupid stuff in a game(s) (probably we need a thread for that as well eheheh), but the difference is that everyone talked about here and on the thread about STs is that they insist on being like that, accept no criticism and are impossible to reason with. <br /> <br /> I've been playing RPG for some 12 years or so and I've done a lot of the stuff described here, no shame to admit it, but every time I was called to attention I made sure I'd improve and try to avoid the mistakes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2435-prophet","name":"Prophet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2435_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-24T09:07:04-08:00","id":380152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just John, Forever...</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/303168-bitching-about-players-thread?p=339082#post339082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah... that dude sounded like he had issues. (PCs killing/diablerizing other PCs, while I've seen it occur in some rare games over the past going on 25 years, is something that usually leaves a bad taste in people's mouths... so to speak...; couple with his other actions, it's amazing his characters hadn't died earlier in their respective scenarios. And the Toreador losing an arm? Sure, for the *character* that would be annoying as hell, but on the player level he should have been like &quot;Wow -- that's it? -- [Character name] sure lucked out on that one...&quot;, especially as -- barring a couple Thaumaturgical/high-end Vicissitude powers, the RAW allow him to regenerate the arm fairly easily, barring being in torpor and without blood.) Sounds like a dick. Did he ever game with you/your people again? (Just curious...)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can't stand playing vampire with my local group. They all essentially play Sabbat even if its cam or anarch or even VtR. Killing and diablerizing whoever they feel the urge to. I mean sure, you expect some double crossing in VtM but someone trying to diablerize another character out of the clear blue because they have a discipline they want and trying to do it during downtime is a few steps too far. and by a few I mean all of the steps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-24T09:17:40-08:00","id":380180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/303168-bitching-about-players-thread?p=305994#post305994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Our boat owner is at least very moe young lass with a cute small crocodile as a pet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hibiki owns a boat?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-24T20:28:01-08:00","id":380715,"title":"","content":"Actually, today Banality felled on me.<br /> <br /> There's this guy who I taught to be a Storyteller, and then he began to hold his own chronicles. About a year and a half ago, I needed a fourth player for my chronicle (the previous one moved away) and then he entered in the chronicle. After three or four months I realized that there was something wrong and we talked about it; it was almost as if during the sessions he was bored, but nevertheless insists on playing. Then he told me that he didn't get a good vibe from his character; therefore I tried to meet him halfway, suggesting different evolutionary paths for the character, to make him feel like his own, more personal.<br /> Frankly, the problem was also mine because I don't feel very motivated without reactive players. It's almost like playing alone.<br /> Everything ok for 3-4 months, then the same problem. We talk about it, I give others ideas. We continue to play.<br /> 3-4 months, the problem returns. We discuss another time, and I ask him if he want to make a new character. No, he does not like the idea of losing the hard-won experience points, he think that would create hardships for the other players and basically he believes that a different character would overlap with the roles of the other PC (I have never seen the problem, but that's not the issue here). Eventually, after enumerating my significant deficiencies he promises that he will try again with his character, more motivated.<br /> Another 3-4 months, now. Still the same problem. I'm tired of the situation and I'm going to talk just because we are friends and I care a lot for the chronicle, as it lasted more than two years and therefore I would like to complete it. This time I decided to pressure him, at the cost of being unpleasant, because I really want to understand what the hell is the problem. Finally, after three hours of discussions, he admits the real problem.<br /> He is annoyed by how I set the chronicle (tons of NPC, relevance to the canon, metaplot, etc), he barely tolerate the system of rules that I use (essentially, the houserules I use and the rules I should ignore and do not), and basically the only true reason why he still plays with us is that he really likes the company.<br /> <br /> At this point, I must probably be angry, because he could at least trouble himself and tell me before ... but I'm just disappointed. Indeed, it is from yesterday that I have a sort of rejection for all role-playing games in general, and in particular for my chronicle. The desire to complete this chronicle I worked on for over two and a half years is completely gone, almost as if someone drained it.<br /> <br /> I feel like I lost the spark. Welcome, Banality.<br /> <br /> [Sorry for the sad note on this topic.]<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":515,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","user":"Ryoga84","date":". 01-24-2015, 11:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T06:34:48-08:00","id":380929,"title":"","content":"@Ryoga84 feel bad for you mate :/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2435-prophet","name":"Prophet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2435_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T04:11:56-08:00","id":381732,"title":"","content":"Thanks, bro <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T04:28:28-08:00","id":381745,"title":"","content":"Goddamnit, a frenzied vampire / draugr close and one of player had in mind to split and chase after a ghost or something. Good she dropped that idea, but man, I would report her to our handler from Cheiron Group.<br /> <br /> Though, if the character of that player dies, I will ask my character's surgeon to make implants of her because psychic powers are cool.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T05:24:17-08:00","id":381805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryoga84</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/303168-bitching-about-players-thread?p=380715#post380715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At this point, I must probably be angry, because he could at least trouble himself and tell me before ... but I'm just disappointed. Indeed, it is from yesterday that I have a sort of rejection for all role-playing games in general, and in particular for my chronicle. The desire to complete this chronicle I worked on for over two and a half years is completely gone, almost as if someone drained it.<br /> <br /> I feel like I lost the spark. Welcome, Banality.<br /> <br /> [Sorry for the sad note on this topic.]</div> </div> </div> </div>I second prophet's sentiment.<br /> <br /> On the other band the other players look like they are enjoying it too...which is great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T14:23:18-08:00","id":402453,"title":"","content":"Alright, I've had it with this player before the game even started. His attitude. His actions. His arrogance. Makes me not just kick him out but burn the W20 game I spent 4 months setting up.<br /> <br /> I decided to run Werewolf where I live because everyone is running either D&amp;D or Pathfinder. I decided I would drudge up an old Werewolf idea I have wanted to do for awhile and finally getting the W20 Core, I thought yes! Let's do it! I just got off running a good Mage: The Ascension Revised game before I moved here. <br /> <br /> This is the kind of game, I love, the SL I have is going to be great. I built Colorado as a giant sandbox with lots of dangling threads for the party taking 4 months to design. 2 of the players already have played with me. So I am just recruiting new blood and that is what I did. So let's call him <b>New Cub</b>. <br /> <br /> <b>New Cub</b> had one WoD experience and did not like it. Hey happens. He had no real experience with Werewolf (a plus I thought at the time) but was willing to learn. <br /> <br /> Now I prefer to follow what WoD suggests especially when running Werewolf. Get the group together and everyone work on their characters together. Discuss their characters. Work on the Pack and Pack Totem etc. <br /> <br /> <b>New Cub</b> asks me tons of Q's and I answered them quickly with page numbers and rules clarifications as well as themes of the game and Tribes. I even passed him my book to read. I own a digital copy so he could use my physical to go through. I already had what I needed and worked out. I own a damned library of WoD books of Vampire, Werewolf and Mage and thankfully my wife is happy I have them as she games too. <br /> <br /> I made this clear to <b>New Cub</b> and all my other players that I wanted to do a sit down and design phase. This is different from other games. I want everyone to work together for character creation. Come in with your ideas. I told all of them I added in some CC additional rules (I give a free bonus in Totem and 3 more Background Points) but they did not know that. I would have CC rules and such at the game. <br /> <br /> <b>New Cub</b> decided to build his character all the way through and write a background. All of which I told no one to do. We had Prelude things to do. Go through First Changes. Etc. I told everyone this in email and in person. <b>New Cub </b>builds his PC and not knowing cWoD of course made mistakes and did not understand things as well as he thought. I told him his mistakes and told him we will be building at game after we work out Pack and Characters. I cited the Pages for him to review. <br /> <br /> He sent me a background, which I ignored because we had not had our first game session and told him that. I told him hold off don't build a PC and pigeon hold yourself to what you want. There are other players and you as a group need to work out ideas. <br /> <br /> Well it turns out he got someone else to do the same thing he did... <br /> <br /> So I get to my first game and I start sitting back asking people about their concepts. He is there working on his character sheet... ignoring me. When I asked questions to him and the other player they toss me their character sheets. You know the Questions like who are you,. What are you. Etc. I have my PC building packets with me. We need to have an idea to do all that fun stuff for first game. <br /> <br /> Well <b>New Cub </b>starts talking over everyone and telling me that his Glass Walker would go to none of the Moots. His character is not leaving the house. Ever... The game the Glass Walkers rule Denver and thus the State... so he is talking his character is a Hacker Genius Doogie Hooser Type and everyone needs him etc. He tells me that he will never go out with the Pack to fight the Wyrm because he is too weak (he choose a 1 STR) for this Homid Glass Walker. He is telling me and all the other players he is not working with anyone including me because he has a fully written character sheet and background why should he suffer because no one else has a fully developed character like him. <br /> <br /> Of course over half of what he is saying and such shows his lack of knowledge of Werewolf, his concept and his Tribe. He is telling me and speaking over me, the ST, I mean speaking over me like an arrogant know it all prick who knows nothing really of the game how it is going to be. <br /> <br /> He bullied the other players at the table ordering them around and me like we are to serve him. <br /> <br /> I am a pretty lax ST, I like to have player input. I like to work with the players etc. This was completely out of line and when he left early because he had to be somewhere else. I had to pick up the pieces. <br /> <br /> So because of <b>New Cub</b> I sat back thought about what happened and I sent a general email out saying we are starting over this upcoming week. We are going to do it my way or the highway. That because of the lack of respect that was shown to each other in the group and the ST, I am now forced to make this a dictatorship. I am the ST not the players speaking. This kind of actions will not be tolerated and I am bringing a gavel (no joke, it is a wooden toy hammer to my daughter's toy she no longer plays with).<br /> <br /> Yes, Harsh Email but as an ST, that is my job. I am the one in the end running the game. If I had to drag people down or they leave so be it. I am here to make it fun and a bully and the group's overall lack of maturity and consideration that game was astonishing. In 24 years I have never seen anything like that. <br /> <br /> So I put down the rules. Mentioned we will go over etiquette with one another. Etc. When someone is speaking we listen we do not interrupt each other and the ST especially. <br /> <br /> Well he sent me a response telling me how I should run my game and did not like what I wrote <b>(I mentioned no names. I mentioned all the problems that happened. Only person mentioned was myself, where I felt I failed my players and I am not letting that happen again). </b><br /> <br /> He sends me a response telling me how to run my game. How he should not be held back by the party because some people had not made or formed ideas yet. Etc. He was the only one with a truly formed out idea and they should be working with him not the other way around. And he can't handle a ST that is bringing in a Dictatorship that this is the Storyteller system etc. <br /> <br /> Tonight when I get home. I am sending him an email kicking his ass out. I don't give a damn that he runs one of the big local RPG Meet Up Groups in town. I don't give a damn he will bad mouth me because of what I am going to do. If no one wants to play with me because he is that kind of arrogant asshole so be it. <br /> <br /> I am not compromising my players, my obligation to them as a ST to bring a fun and entertaining game each session, because someone is trying to bully me. If it does not stop here. It will just get worse. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4949-nene-richards","name":"Nene Richards","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4949_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T17:58:46-08:00","id":402676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nene Richards</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/303168-bitching-about-players-thread?p=402453#post402453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, Harsh Email but as an ST, that is my job. I am the one in the end running the game. If I had to drag people down or they leave so be it. I am here to make it fun and a bully and the group's overall lack of maturity and consideration that game was astonishing. In 24 years I have never seen anything like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually in a vaguely similar situation myself, albeit from the other side (no, I'm not getting into it). Now, I don't presume to know the whole situation, for all I know it's exactly as you describe.<br /> <br /> But the way you write about it concerns me. Yeah, seems like this player is a problem, but on the other hand it does seem like you've taken a very &quot;my way or the highway&quot; approach right from the get-go, and that pretty much never works out long- or even medium-term. It discourages the players from working <i>with</i> you, and RPing, at least WW games, is all about co-operation. Now, from what you say New Cub is out of line, no disputing that. But on the other hand, if the other players are doing as you describe, and these guys are more experienced players, then it seems unlikely for him to be the only problem. I mean, one player can disrupt things, but a new player has very little in the way of leverage to push others into doing what they want, so unless he's either really eloquent, or threatening them with violence, or they're just incredible doormats (being RPers, not out of the question), I very much doubt it's all New Cub's doing.<br /> <br /> As I said, I don't know your situation beyond what you've said, so I'm speaking generally here. But the fact that you have, from what you described, constantly tried to deal with the situation through exerting <i>control</i> rather than <i>compromise</i>, doesn't sound like a workable solution. Often I find that the most successful STs throw the player a bone and ask the player to do the same. As an example (not saying this would have worked specifically): &quot;I see that you have a strong character concept worked out ahead of time. I'm glad you're excited about the game, but Werewolf is primarily a game about werewolf packs, which means working together, which is why I wanted to do character creation together, so peoples characters can complement each other a bit better. Now, the hacker concept is good, and there's a lot of story stuff I can work with with that, but it seems a bit restrictive; never leaving the house is going to seriously limit how much you can actually participate. How about you throw in some social skills, and he can also help support the pack through shmoozing and asking people questions, gathering information that way as well?&quot;<br /> <br /> Or, you know, something.<br /> <br /> Obviously, New Cub is out of line. But I don't think that the trouble is entirely down to him; from what you describe your management of the situation seems a bit sub-optimal. I'd tentatively suggest mentioning at the start of the next session that you want the game to be fun for everyone, which means co-operation, and you'd like to pursue that pathway rather than hammering people going outside your expectations.<br /> <br /> I mean, after all. You can tell a story by yourself, but that's hardly as fun as telling it <i>with</i> people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T19:28:11-08:00","id":402779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/303168-bitching-about-players-thread?p=402676#post402676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm actually in a vaguely similar situation myself, albeit from the other side (no, I'm not getting into it). Now, I don't presume to know the whole situation, for all I know it's exactly as you describe.<br /> <br /> But the way you write about it concerns me. Yeah, seems like this player is a problem, but on the other hand it does seem like you've taken a very &quot;my way or the highway&quot; approach right from the get-go, and that pretty much never works out long- or even medium-term. It discourages the players from working <i>with</i> you, and RPing, at least WW games, is all about co-operation. Now, from what you say New Cub is out of line, no disputing that. But on the other hand, if the other players are doing as you describe, and these guys are more experienced players, then it seems unlikely for him to be the only problem. I mean, one player can disrupt things, but a new player has very little in the way of leverage to push others into doing what they want, so unless he's either really eloquent, or threatening them with violence, or they're just incredible doormats (being RPers, not out of the question), I very much doubt it's all New Cub's doing.<br /> <br /> As I said, I don't know your situation beyond what you've said, so I'm speaking generally here. But the fact that you have, from what you described, constantly tried to deal with the situation through exerting <i>control</i> rather than <i>compromise</i>, doesn't sound like a workable solution. Often I find that the most successful STs throw the player a bone and ask the player to do the same. As an example (not saying this would have worked specifically): &quot;I see that you have a strong character concept worked out ahead of time. I'm glad you're excited about the game, but Werewolf is primarily a game about werewolf packs, which means working together, which is why I wanted to do character creation together, so peoples characters can complement each other a bit better. Now, the hacker concept is good, and there's a lot of story stuff I can work with with that, but it seems a bit restrictive; never leaving the house is going to seriously limit how much you can actually participate. How about you throw in some social skills, and he can also help support the pack through shmoozing and asking people questions, gathering information that way as well?&quot;<br /> <br /> Or, you know, something.<br /> <br /> Obviously, New Cub is out of line. But I don't think that the trouble is entirely down to him; from what you describe your management of the situation seems a bit sub-optimal. I'd tentatively suggest mentioning at the start of the next session that you want the game to be fun for everyone, which means co-operation, and you'd like to pursue that pathway rather than hammering people going outside your expectations.<br /> <br /> I mean, after all. You can tell a story by yourself, but that's hardly as fun as telling it <i>with</i> people.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I love player input. I had no problem talking to the players about their ideas. I explained things if they were thinking of something. I am pretty laid back. I don't toss in the strong arm card. I sent information when asked. In what I described with <b>New Cub</b> I was answering everyone else's questions. I tailor my games around my players why I build a sandbox to begin with to let the players dictate which thread works best for them.<br /> <br /> I want to ask you something:<br /> <br /> Is speaking over people even shouting over them and telling them they are wrong before they finished speaking acceptable to you?<br /> <br /> Is saying you won't work the other players but they have to follow what you tell them to build?<br /> <br /> Do you speaking over your ST as he is explaining something because you don't like it correcting him and you do not know what you are talking about like how much Garou handle the Umbra?<br /> <br /> Do you treat your other players with complete disrespect?<br /> <br /> Do you throw a fit if you don't get your way?<br /> <br /> Do you insult the ST with saying he/she does not know what they are talking about to their face even when they show you they were right?<br /> <br /> That is <b>New Cub</b>. That was not me. He was completely rude to the whole party and myself. He showed no respect to anyone but expected us to respect him.<br /> <br /> If you find that acceptable fine. I was hoping we could all talk about their characters because only 1 player out of 4 had played werewolf and one player was thinking of joining but since <b>New Cub</b> acted like an asshole the player told me he does not want to play with him.<br /> <br /> You have to be pretty fluid when running a game like Mage, which is something I have been running for over 15 years. I have been running WoD for 24. Took me years to finally grasp Mage to where I thought I could run it.<br /> <br /> Saying we were not respecting each other and I let it out of hand. I agree that was my mistake. Saying I am rigid. That I am not. If you sat in that room, you would have felt the same. I never experienced something like this in 24 plus years of gaming.<br /> <br /> I tell everyone when I recruit I am out to make a fun game. I explained my ST style to everyone. I even had it up on my website. My managing a game has never been an issue. I have been asking around about <b>New Cub</b> I am working a charity event with a bunch of gamers on a food drive. They told me they dont game with him for the same reasons... <br /> <br /> My job is managing and organizing for a living. I am a community engagement specialist. Dealing with people is what I do for a living. I never had a parent ever act this way,.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4949-nene-richards","user":"Nene Richards","date":". 02-11-2015, 10:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4949-nene-richards","name":"Nene Richards","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4949_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}